#: ../../source/foundations.rst:2
msgid "Foundations"
msgstr "基础"

#: ../../source/foundations.rst:4
msgid ""
"Diátaxis is successful because it *works* - both users and creators have a "
"better experience of documentation as a result. It makes sense and it feels "
"right."
msgstr "Diátaxis 的成功之处在于它 *行之有效*。无论是用户还是创作者，都会由此获得更好的文档体验。它既合乎情理，又符合直觉。"

#: ../../source/foundations.rst:6
msgid ""
"However, that's not enough to be confident in Diátaxis as a theory of "
"documentation. As a theory, it needs to show *why* it works. It needs to "
"show that there is actually some reason why there are exactly four kinds of "
"documentation, not three or five. It needs to demonstrate rigorous thinking "
"and analysis, and that it stands on a sound theoretical foundation."
msgstr ""
"然而，仅凭这些，尚不足以让人树立对 Diátaxis 作为文档理论的信心。作为理论，它需要阐明自己 *为何* "
"行之有效。它需要展示，文档之所以恰好分为四类，既不是三类，也不是五类，背后到底存在何种缘由。它还需展现缜密的思辨与剖析，并证明自身立于坚实的理论基础之上。"

#: ../../source/foundations.rst:8
msgid ""
"Otherwise, it will be just another useful heuristic approach, and the "
"strongest claim we can make for it is that \"it seems to work quite well\"."
msgstr "否则，它便不过是另一种可资借鉴的方法，我们最多只能称其为“看起来行之有效”。"

#: ../../source/foundations.rst:12
msgid "Two dimensions of craft"
msgstr "技艺的两个维度"

#: ../../source/foundations.rst:14
msgid ""
"Diátaxis is based on the principle that documentation must serve the needs "
"of its users. Knowing how to do that means understanding what the needs of "
"users are."
msgstr "Diátaxis 基于这样一项原则：文档必须服务于用户的需求。要知道如何做到这一点，便需要理解用户的需求是什么。"

#: ../../source/foundations.rst:16
msgid ""
"The user whose needs Diátaxis serves is *the practitioner in a domain of "
"skill*. A domain of skill is defined by a craft - the use of a tool or "
"product is a craft. So is an entire discipline or profession. Using a "
"programming language is a craft, as is flying a particular aircraft, or even"
" being a pilot in general."
msgstr ""
"Diátaxis 所服务的用户，是 "
"*技能领域中的实践者*。技能领域由一门技艺所界定——工具或产品的使用即是一门技艺。整个学科或专业皆是如此。使用编程语言是一门技艺，驾驶特定型号的飞机亦然，乃至广义上担任一名飞行员亦是如此。"

#: ../../source/foundations.rst:18
msgid ""
"Understanding the needs of these users means in turn understanding the "
"essential characteristics of craft or skill."
msgstr "要理解这些用户的需求，便须进而把握技艺或技能的基本特性。"

#: ../../source/foundations.rst:22
msgid "Action/cognition"
msgstr "行动 / 认知"

#: ../../source/foundations.rst:24
msgid ""
"A skill or craft or practice contains both **action** (practical knowledge, "
"knowing *how*, what we do) and **cognition** (theoretical knowledge, knowing"
" *that*, what we think). The two are completely bound up with each other, "
"but they are counterparts, wholly distinct from each other, two different "
"aspects of the same thing."
msgstr ""
"一项技能、技艺或实践活动，都兼具 **行动**（实践知识，即知道如何做，也就是我们所做的）与 "
"**认知**（理论知识，即知道是什么，也就是我们所想的）两个层面。两者紧密交织，却交相辉映，彼此之间截然不同，一体两面。"

#: ../../source/foundations.rst:28
msgid "Acquisition/application"
msgstr "习得 / 运用"

#: ../../source/foundations.rst:30
msgid ""
"Similarly, the relationship of a practitioner with their practice is that it"
" is something that needs to be both **acquired**, and **applied**. Being "
"\"at work\" (concerned with applying the skill and knowledge of their craft)"
" and being \"at study\" (concerned with acquiring them) are once again "
"counterparts, distinct but bound up with each other."
msgstr ""
"同样，实践者与其实践的关系，体现为实践本身既要 **习得**，也要 **运用**。所谓 “工作状态”（关注于运用技艺的知识与技能）与 "
"“学习状态”（关注于习得这些知识与技能）同样是相互对应的关系，彼此截然不同，却又紧密交织。"

#: ../../source/foundations.rst:34
msgid "The map of the territory"
msgstr "领域地图"

#: ../../source/foundations.rst:36
msgid ""
"This gives us two dimensions of skill, that we can lay out on a map - a map "
"of the territory of craft:"
msgstr "由此我们得到技能的两个维度，我们可将其呈现于一张地图之上——即技艺领域的地图："

#: ../../source/foundations.rst:38 ../../source/foundations.rst:51
msgid "The territory of craft as a two-dimensional map"
msgstr "技艺领域的二维地图"

#: ../../source/foundations.rst:41
msgid ""
"This is a *complete* map. There are only two dimensions, and they don't just"
" cover the entire territory, they define it. This is why there are "
"necessarily four quarters to it, and there could not be three, or five. It "
"is not an arbitrary number."
msgstr ""
"这是一张 *完整* "
"的地图。它所包含的维度仅有这两个，但它们不仅覆盖了整个领域，更界定了领域本身。这便是为何它必然划分为四个象限，而非三个或五个。这个数字并非随意而定。"

#: ../../source/foundations.rst:43
msgid ""
"It also shows us the *qualities* of craft that define each of them. When the"
" idea that documentation must serve the needs of craft is applied to this "
"map, it reveals in turn what documentation must be and do to fulfil those "
"obligations - in four distinct ways."
msgstr ""
"它也向我们展示了技艺的 "
"*特质*，这些特质定义了每一个象限。当“文档必须服务于技艺需求”这一理念被运用于这张地图时，它便反过来昭示出，文档必须以四种各异的途径成其所是，行其所为，方能践行这一理念。"

#: ../../source/foundations.rst:47
msgid "Serving needs"
msgstr "服务于需求"

#: ../../source/foundations.rst:49
msgid ""
"The map of the territory of craft is what gives us the familiar Diátaxis map"
" of documentation. The map is in effect an answer to the question: what must"
" documentation do to align with these qualities of skill, and to what need "
"is it oriented in each case?"
msgstr ""
"我们熟悉的 Diátaxis "
"文档地图，便源自这张技艺领域的地图。它实质上是对以下问题的回应：文档必须做到什么，才能与技能的这些性质相协调，而针对每一种情况，它又需要服务于何种需求？"

#: ../../source/foundations.rst:54
msgid ""
"We can see how the map of documentation addresses *needs* across those two "
"dimensions, each need also defined by the characteristics of its quarter of "
"the map."
msgstr "我们可以看出，在这两个维度上，文档处理的需求是如何分布的。而每个需求也同样由其所在象限的特征所界定。"

